<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ramiro de Lorqua</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1502</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Remirro de Orco</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ramiro de Lorqua was a Spanish captain in the service of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesare-borgia">Cesare Borgia</a>, who made him governor of the newly conquered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romagna">Romagna</a> in 1501. He restored order with great harshness, and in December 1502 Cesare had him arrested and executed, displaying his body in the main square of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cesena">Cesena</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-machiavelli">Machiavelli</a>, who witnessed the events, described the episode in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/the-prince">The Prince</a> as a lesson in how a ruler may use and then disown a cruel minister.</p></div>
